1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,952
This bottle says vitamin B2. Inside is chalk.

2
00:00:03,972 --> 00:00:07,564
Watch the blue line: the water clouds, the light drops,

3
00:00:07,584 --> 00:00:09,229
right into the reference band.

4
00:00:09,249 --> 00:00:12,013
A one-sensor tester would call that a pass.

5
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,002
But the green line never moves.

6
00:00:14,022 --> 00:00:18,567
Pill says NEEDS LAB, and the supplier’s $480 stays held,

7
00:00:18,587 --> 00:00:21,950
sandbox money, with a lab referral already drafted.

8
00:00:30,850 --> 00:00:34,067
One tablet, one cup, 60 seconds.

9
00:00:34,067 --> 00:00:37,926
The board streams light readings once a second; the app decides.

10
00:00:37,926 --> 00:00:46,650
Three answers only: Passed the screen · Needs lab testing · Unable to verify

11
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,837
WHO estimates 1 in 10 medical products in low- and middle-income countries

12
00:00:52,857 --> 00:00:54,250
is substandard or falsified.

13
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:58,378
A new lab dissolution tester costs $20,000 to $100,000,

14
00:00:58,398 --> 00:01:01,299
and lab results take 7 to 10 business days.

15
00:01:01,319 --> 00:01:03,437
A clinic pharmacist has neither.

16
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:06,840
Pill is a $40 box.

17
00:01:06,860 --> 00:01:11,304
One quarter tablet, about three minutes, two channels that must agree.

18
00:01:11,324 --> 00:01:13,929
Riboflavin absorbs blue and glows green.

19
00:01:13,949 --> 00:01:15,680
Chalk only blocks light.

20
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:18,565
It says three things only:

21
00:01:18,585 --> 00:01:21,579
PASS, NEEDS LAB, UNABLE TO VERIFY.

22
00:01:21,599 --> 00:01:22,678
Never a fourth.

23
00:01:22,698 --> 00:01:27,308
Seven fixed rules set the verdict; Claude only writes the two-sentence why.

24
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:31,143
Here is the app, replaying the chalk run.

25
00:01:31,163 --> 00:01:34,784
The pill fills against the reference, the glow bar stays dark,

26
00:01:34,804 --> 00:01:37,677
and the card stamps NEEDS LAB, rule N2.

27
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:42,595
A riboflavin lot passes, rule P1.

28
00:01:42,615 --> 00:01:44,979
The policy agent proposes release,

29
00:01:44,999 --> 00:01:47,977
and only the pharmacist’s press-and-hold moves the money.

30
00:01:47,997 --> 00:01:50,222
Every decision is one log line.

31
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:55,422
In clinic mode, the invoice waits in escrow.

32
00:01:55,442 --> 00:01:57,946
NEEDS LAB holds it and drafts a lab referral.

33
00:01:57,966 --> 00:02:00,655
UNABLE TO VERIFY escalates to a person.

34
00:02:00,675 --> 00:02:03,090
A PASS and a pharmacist’s tap release it.

35
00:02:03,110 --> 00:02:05,650
It’s all sandbox and testnet money today.

36
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:10,104
Every station sells its verdict over x402.

37
00:02:10,124 --> 00:02:13,875
Ask without paying, and you get a 402 with the price:

38
00:02:13,895 --> 00:02:17,093
5 cents of test USDC on Base Sepolia.

39
00:02:17,113 --> 00:02:18,988
Pay it, and you get the verdict;

40
00:02:19,008 --> 00:02:22,175
our paid call is waiting on a test-USDC key.

41
00:02:22,195 --> 00:02:25,700
Our agent buys verdicts too, under a $1 daily cap.

42
00:02:26,950 --> 00:02:31,681
Live today: Gemini reading the label, Claude’s sentences and escrow clerk,

43
00:02:31,701 --> 00:02:34,520
the seven rules, and the real 402.

44
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:38,791
Simulated or pending: the escrow transfers, the paid 200,

45
00:02:38,811 --> 00:02:41,738
the station hardware, and these replayed curves.

46
00:02:41,758 --> 00:02:43,465
Every screen says which.

47
00:02:44,950 --> 00:02:48,986
Our workflow runs from code: the repo writes one deck.json,

48
00:02:49,006 --> 00:02:51,573
and our Figma plugin turns it into Slides.

49
00:02:51,593 --> 00:02:54,097
Each stage is in our Figma stage log.

50
00:02:55,150 --> 00:02:58,098
Pill. Try to make it say PASS on the chalk.
